 "correction": "The HUD aspect system was whitelisted to Quake III and RTCW in two places: the client enablement and the root-archive allowlist that decides which files the package may serve. Elite Force reached neither, so its cgame draws were stretched with the frame and a rules file would not have loaded. Both now include Elite Force, and each profile ships rules authored from the draw groups its retail modules actually issued. Separately, no Elite Force map had an audio zone sidecar; the zone compiler now accepts both profiles as the IBSP 46 Quake fork they are, and every official map has one.",
